{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"A6-0b oracle card (strong-tier, pre-code). Authoritative contract: signed ticket plan at 019e32e03d plus docs/concurrency.md union-preservation invariant and A6-0a epoch refusal. Existing coverage: test_reviewbot_ensure_tickets proves initialization/idempotence/failure marker; test_epoch_guard_reconciliation and test_sync_union_recovery prove core reconverge epoch/union behavior; autodeploy script tests provide a real PATH-shim harness; voter tests prove post_vote ordering but lack an emit-failure-after-vote case. Trigger preconditions: single-branch persistent clone; saved local/prior-origin tips; explicit-refspec fetch; pre-epoch local versus epoch-bearing rewritten remote; clean, ahead, diverged, missing-ref, corrupt, and fetch-failure states. Production path: generated entrypoint -> reviewbot-ensure-tickets.sh -> existing sync.reconverge for compatible stores, or narrow under-write-lock adoption of one pinned fetched commit only after proving no local-only commit. Test tier: real temporary Git repos + shell subprocess; unit voter boundary; autodeploy PATH-shim. Exact postconditions: expected HEAD/ref reachability, no lost local/remote event commits, exact refusal preservation, warning/exit contract, no MERGE_HEAD/stash, BOT_PATHS deploy selection. Collateral invariants: index clean, no in-progress merge/rebase, vote remains recorded. Recovery: refused adoption leaves exact local tip for manual handling and a clean retry after safe state converges. Contention: held-out moving-ref test perturbs origin/tickets between validation and reset and requires the pinned commit; no timing sleep. Surface census: operational shell entrypoint in scope; automated review-bot caller in scope; library core in scope via real reconverge; CLI and MCP/API out of scope (no distinct path); dual direction in scope via inbound clone convergence plus outbound post-vote artifact-failure test. Gate: focused pytest nodes, then make lint/typecheck/test. Implementer tier will be standard because this is multi-file Git-state integration; edge/E2E oracle stays held out."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785831439625998001,"uuid":"ba245b1e-5ce6-4765-9e2a-eb354951bdd6"}